This is a major finding. Look at lines **936 and 941** — that's **anti-piracy / anti-tamper code**:

```cpp
bool isHave2 = JniHelper::getStaticMethodInfo(minfo2,"net/zakume/game/NarutoSenki","getCurrentName", ...);
if (isHave2) { ...bag = getCurrentName()... }
else {
    _CharacterArray=NULL;   // ← line 936: class NOT found → sabotage state
}
```

It looks up the Java class **`net/zakume/game/NarutoSenki`** — the *original author's* package. But you repackaged to `dev.leaderone.narutosenki`, so that class **doesn't exist** → `isHave2=false` → it **deliberately nulls `_CharacterArray`**. This is a booby-trap: repackage the game, and it silently corrupts state so it crashes "randomly" later. That's almost certainly the source of your random/settlement crashes.

Let me confirm which function this lives in and whether it runs during gameplay.

